    90	| Theorem K / S″ | the design's split cost p ≥ (γ/4)(γ/(16 log N))^{2k}/(32k²); no C(2k, k), no 2^ω | k enters only as the (by design) L[2/5]-size split cost | Lemma S″ replaces S′ | **0** |
    91	| Lemma CS (computable S) | the old explicit S lost de Bruijn's second-order term (thmA U5), and S^d must be inside X_F | — | Rankin value at an approximate saddle point, evaluated at the actual X_F(S) | **0** |
    92	| LV6 | Stark ν₁ ≍ 1/((2d)! log Δ̄); SQ's 2^{d−1} sign vectors; t_χ = poly(d, log N) | cost only, exp(O(d log d)) = L[2/5]^{o(1)} | factorial-bit character primes | not a γ-loss |
    93	| Lemma IR, rejections | exp(−log H/(13 d log log H)) = exp(−(log N)^{2/5−o(1)}) | no | — | not a γ-loss |
    94	
    95	So α = (2 + 0)/(5 + 0) = 2/5.
