    99	## 1. Parameters and the algorithm FACTOR_U
   100	
   101	**Notation.** For the integer N handed to SPLIT (after preprocessing): λ := log log N, D := log N/λ,
   102	Λ := D^{2/5}λ = (log N)^{2/5}(log log N)^{3/5}, and L_N[2/5, c] = e^{cΛ}. "L^{o(1)}" now means exp(o(Λ)),
   103	uniformly in N. All "C" below depend only on (a, κ, d₀) and on the absolute constants of the cited theorems.
   104	**They never depend on d, k or N.**
   105	
   106	**Fixed parameters.** Rationals a, κ, d₀ > 0.
   107	
   108	**N-dependent parameters** (all computable in time (log N)^{O(1)}, except S, which costs B(log N)^{O(1)}; §2):
   109	- d := the least odd integer ≥ max(3, d₀D^{1/5}); k := max(⌈κD^{2/5}⌉, d + 1); ν := 1/(4k).
   110	- η₀ := 1/⌈D^{1/2}⌉.
   111	- μ := μ_opt(d, k) of [pp] Lemma `lem:optmu` (exact rational); h := h_*(μ) + η₀ with
   112	  h_*(μ) = max(2ν, μ − (d−2)ν, 1 − dμ + ν); θ := 2μ + h + (d−1)ν.
   113	  Then θ·D^{1/5} → θ₀(d₀, κ) := 3/d₀ if κ ≥ d₀²/4, and 2/d₀ + d₀/(4κ) otherwise (`params.theta0`). (At fixed
   114	  d the k-term of the level regime is lower order: 4ν = 1/k ≍ D^{−2/5}.)
   115	- B := ⌊e^{aΛ}⌋. X := ⌊√(N/2)⌋; j maximal with 2^{kj} ≤ X; Y := 2^{j−1}; J := primes in (Y, 2Y]. So
   116	  log Y = log N/(2k) + O(1) = Λ_{3/5}/(2κ)(1 + o(1)), i.e. ℓ = L_N[3/5, 1/(2κ)].
   117	- M := ⌊N^μ⌋, H := ⌊N^h⌋, W := ⌈N^{μ+ν+η₀/2}⌉ (integer roots of N^p for the rational exponents).
   118	- S: the first S = 2^j in the scan j = 0, 1, 2, … with S²·R(X_r(S))·R(X_F(S)) ≥ 1 (Lemma CS), where
   119	  **V(S) := ⌊√(2Y)·S⌋, common to all ℓ ∈ J**, X_r(S) := 2MV/Y and **X_F(S) := (2d + 1)·MHV^d**.
   120	  Put V := V(S), X_r, X_F at this S, ρ_r := ϱ(X_r), ρ_F := ϱ(X_F) (ϱ(z) = Ψ(z, B)/z).
   121	- Candidates (one set for all ℓ): **𝒫 := {(a, b) ∈ Z² : b prime, (1 − 1/d)V < b ≤ V, |a| ≤ V, gcd(a, b) = 1}.**
   122	- Filter: |G(P)| ≥ MV/32. Counted points, N_ℓ(A), descendable set 𝒟_A, δ_A and γ as in [pp] §3.3, with 𝒫 and V.
   123	
   124	The analysis-only parameters (never used by the algorithm): ϖ := B²S² (truncation, FM), the grid
   125	𝒳 := {X_F ϖ^{−2}(3/2)^i} ∩ [X_Fϖ^{−2}, 16dX_F], and R₀ := B^{C₀} with C₀ the least integer such that
   126	B^{C₀} ≥ 64S²B/(ρ_rρ_F) (L2_fam; note the cushion B, not L_N[1/2, 1], following codex lv5unif_1 §1(d)).
   127	
   128	**The algorithm FACTOR_U[a, κ, d₀]** is [pp] Algorithm `alg:factor` (FACTOR, with SPLIT and trial division run in
   129	alternation, so there is no N₀ branch) with SPLIT, SAMPLE_FIELD, DESCEND_ONCE, SQ_SEARCH and POSTPROCESS of [pp]
   130	§3.4 and §8, changed as follows:
   131	1. the parameters above, with the common V and the b-window in 𝒫;
   132	2. DESCEND_ONCE's shape test calls **FACTOR_U itself** on |u₀| and |v₀| with fresh coins (recursion, [rec] §1.1);
   133	3. POSTPROCESS uses character primes of s := ⌈(2d)!·(log N + log Δ̄ + d)⁴⌉ bits (§9);
   134	4. the row target M_rows := C_col + 12 as in [pp] (eq:Mrows), with t_χ of §9.
   135	
   136	The shape test accepts iff |u₀| and |v₀| are each products of at most k distinct primes, all in J, as in [pp].
   137	
   138	*Common V in the special-q search.* In SQ_SEARCH and in [pp] Lemma `lem:reg`, V_ℓ is replaced by V and S by
   139	S_ℓ := V/√ℓ ∈ [S/√2·(1 − o(1)), √2·S]. Lemma `lem:reg` then reads: if λ₁ < √ℓ/(2S_ℓ) = ℓ/(2V), the lattice has no
   140	candidate (the line spacing ℓ/|w₀| exceeds 2V ≥ √2V, and |w₀| < ℓ/(2V) < (1 − 1/d)V < b because ℓ ≤ 2Y < V²/2);
   141	otherwise it has ≤ (8V² + 32λ₂²)/ℓ ≤ 179V²/ℓ ≤ 400S² points in [−V, V]², since λ₂² ≤ (4/3)ℓ²/λ₁² ≤ (16/3)V² and
   142	V² ≤ 2YS². The pair bound of [pp] Lemma `lem:pairs` becomes q = |Δ|/ℓ ≤ 2V²/ℓ ≤ 4S².
   143	
   144	**Lemma P (the parameters are consistent) [proved; leading-order asymptotic arithmetic, encoded in
   145	`params.margins`].** For N ≥ N₀(a, κ, d₀), all of the following hold, each with a ratio that is
   146	exp(c(log N)^p(log log N)^q) with c > 0 and (p, q) > (0, 0); the right-hand "C" is any fixed constant. `params.margins`
   147	encodes these comparisons and the further margins named in §§4–6 and 11 (22 checks after codex lv5unif_2 #6); it
   148	compares leading terms only, and is a check of the notes' arithmetic, not an independent proof:
   149	(P1) Y ≥ B^C; (P2) N^{η₀/4} ≥ B^C, ≥ S^C, ≥ 2^{Cd}; (P3) u_F := log X_F/log B ≥ (log log N)^4; (P4) d log d ≤ Λ/C;
   150	(P5) d log S = o(θ log N) and η₀ = o(θ); (P6) log Y ≥ ω(N) log 2 + C log log N, since ω(N) ≤ log N/log B;
   151	(P7) log H/(13d log log H) ≥ C log log N; (P8) μ − ν ≥ η₀ and h − 2ν ≥ η₀ and h − μ + (d−2)ν ≥ η₀;
   152	(P9) 2S² < Y, B < V/2, V < ℓ; (P10) H ≥ dV²·N^{η₀/2}, H ≥ 3dϖ·V, M/V ≥ N^{η₀/2}.
   153	*Proof.* (P8) is the definition of h and the size μ ≈ 1/d ≫ ν + η₀. The others are the listed comparisons of
   154	leading terms: for example, (P1) compares log Y ≍ (log N)^{3/5}(log log N)^{2/5} with log B ≍ (log N)^{2/5}(log log N)^{3/5};
   155	(P2) compares η₀ log N = (log N log log N)^{1/2} with Λ; (P4) compares d log d ≍ (log N)^{1/5}(log log N)^{4/5} with Λ;
   156	(P6) compares log Y with log N/log B ≍ (log N)^{3/5}(log log N)^{−3/5}. ∎
