   252	
   253	## 4. Theorem FM-U (the first moment, explicit and uniform)
   254	
   255	**Lemma SM1 (one-point smoothing) [proved in [pp] Lemma `lem:smooth1`; uniformity checked].** For P = (a, b) with
   256	gcd(a, b) = 1, ab ≠ 0, V′ := max(|a|, |b|), H ≥ 3dV′: there is a probability measure ϑ on Z with
   257	TV(Law⟨c, v(P)⟩, ϑ) ≤ 3d²V′/(2H + 1), ϑ = Law(Σ Y_i) with Y_i independent uniform on integer intervals of lengths
   258	(2H + 1)l_i (l_i = |a|^{d−1−i}|b|^i), ϑ symmetric unimodal about M₀ with |M₀| ≤ dV′^{d−1}, and
   259	max ϑ ≤ 1/((2H + 1)V′^{d−1}).
   260	*Uniformity check.* Every constant in that proof is explicit and polynomial in d: the kernel basis u_j = be_j − ae_{j+1}
   261	has ℓ^∞-cells of radius |a| + |b|; the d smoothing shifts have ℓ^∞-size ≤ 3V′; the total-variation cost is
   262	d·3dV′/(2H + 1); log-concavity is dimension-free. The exponentially large *cardinality* of the smoothing sets is
   263	neither a probability loss nor a cost (they are analysis devices). This replaces LV Lemmas 5.13, 5.18 and 5.20
   264	(LV §5 is the growing-degree model; we need none of its L^{o(1)}-precision statements). ∎
   265	
   266	**Lemma GM-U (algebraic smoothness at a good modulus) [proved].** Let ℓ ∈ J, P = (a, b) ∈ 𝒫, g ∈ 𝒢 and w be such that
   267	t := |G(P)| ∈ [MV/32, 2MV], t is good ([pp] Definition `def:good`, with the grid 𝒳 of §1), and
   268	r₀ := F̂_{g,w}(P) mod t is a unit. Then Pr_c[F_A(P) ∈ 𝒮_B] ≥ ρ_F/(log N)^{C_g}, with C_g = C(a, κ, d₀).
   269	
   270	*Proof.* [pp] Lemma `lem:goodmod`, with these explicit inputs.
   271	- V′ ∈ ((1 − 1/d)V, V], so V′^{d−1} ≥ V^{d−1}/e; Y_ϖ := (2H + 1)V′^{d−1}/ϖ; |M₀| ≤ dV′^{d−1} ≤ Y_ϖ/2 by (P10).
   272	- Small layers have ϑ-mass ≤ 3/ϖ.
   273	- **Norm envelope.** By [pp] Lemma `lem:valuesizes`, |F̂(P)| ≤ 2^{2d+5}MHV^dN^{−η₀/2} ≤ MHV^dN^{−η₀/4} by (P2).
   274	  This is the only place the exponential constant of the base expansion occurs, and it is absorbed here.
   275	  Every value F̂ + Gz with |z| ≤ dHV^{d−1} has absolute value ≤ (2d + 1)MHV^d = X_F.
   276	- One large layer: ty′ ≥ (MV/32)(Y_ϖ/2 − 1) ≥ MHV^d/(64eϖ) ≥ 4|F̂| by (P2); ty′/4 ≥ X_Fϖ^{−2} because
   277	  ϖ ≥ 256e(2d + 1); ty′/2 ≤ 16dX_F. So some x₁ ∈ 𝒳 lies in (ty′/4, ty′/2].
   278	- Good t and Tenenbaum's theorem (ω(t) ≤ log N; [pp] Fact `fact:Ten`) give
   279	  Ψ(x₁; t, r′) ≥ Ψ_t(x₁)/(2φ(t)) ≥ Ψ(x₁)/(3t) ≥ (y′/12)ϱ(x₁). Here X_F/B^{C₁} ≤ x₁ ≤ 16dX_F ≤ BX_F, with
   280	  C₁ := ⌈σ/a⌉ + 3 fixed (since X_F/x₁ ≤ 256e(2d + 1)ϖ). If x₁ ≤ X_F, Lemma U1(i) gives ϱ(x₁) ≥ ϱ(X_F)/2; if
   281	  x₁ > X_F, Lemma U1(ii) gives ϱ(x₁) ≥ ϱ(X_F)(log N)^{−2C_U}. Either way ϱ(x₁) ≥ ρ_F/(log N)^{2C_U}.
   282	- The error terms: (|F̂|/t + 1)/y ≤ 33eϖN^{−η₀/4} and 3d²V/(2H + 1) ≤ N^{−η₀}, both ≤ ρ_F·B^{−1} by (P2), (P10).
   283	  So the proportion of smooth values in each large layer is ≥ ρ_F/(24(log N)^{2C_U}) − 33eϖN^{−η₀/4} (each half
   284	  [0, y′], [−y′, 0] contributes y′ϱ(x₁)/12 of the 2y + 1 points), and
   285	  Pr_c ≥ (1 − 3/ϖ)(ρ_F/(24(log N)^{2C_U}) − 33eϖN^{−η₀/4}) − N^{−η₀} ≥ ρ_F/(log N)^{C_g}, C_g := 2C_U + 5. ∎
   286	
   287	**Lemma FIB (fibres) [proved in [pp] Lemma `lem:fibres`, with V_ℓ := V].** |𝒢_P(n)| ≤ 2M/V for every n; there is an
   288	interval I_P of length ≥ MV/(16ℓ) − 1 on which ℓn has constant sign, MV/32 ≤ ℓ|n| ≤ 2MV and
   289	|𝒢_P(n)| ≥ M/(CV log log N). The Möbius error is 2^{ω(ℓ|n|)} ≤ exp(O(log N·μ/log log N)) ≤ (M/V)^{o(1)} (codex's
   290	corrected form), which is negligible against M/V ≥ N^{η₀/2}. ∎
   291	
   292	**Theorem FM-U [proved].** For N ≥ N₀(a, κ, d₀),
   293	  E_{ℓ∈J}E_{A∼𝒜}N_ℓ(A) ≥ S²ρ_rρ_F/(d·(log N)^{C_FM}),  C_FM = C(a, κ, d₀).
   294	
   295	*Proof.* [pp] Theorem `thm:FM`, with:
   296	- The primes of J dividing N are dropped; there are at most log N/log Y ≤ 2k of them, a fraction ≤ 2k/π_J of J
   297	  (Opus proof critic #6; [pp] says O(1) at fixed k).
   298	- #𝒫 ≥ V·(V/(2d log V)): primes in ((1 − 1/d)V, V] number ≥ V/(2d log V) by the prime number theorem with
   299	  de la Vallée Poussin's error term, since 1/d ≥ exp(−c√(log V)) (log V ≍ (log N)^{3/5}(log log N)^{2/5}); each b
   300	  has ≥ V coprime a with |a| ≤ V.
   301	- Good mass: for each P, Σ_{n∈I_P∩𝒮_B}|𝒢_P(n)| ≥ cM²ρ_r/(ℓ log log N), by Lemma U1(iii) and FIB. With
   302	  ℓ ≤ 2Y and V² ≥ YS² this gives a contribution ≥ cS²ρ_rρ_F/(d log V log log N (log N)^{C_g}).
   303	- Bad mass: the moduli ℓ|n| lie in 𝒯_Q for the 7 dyadic Q covering [MV/32, 2MV] (one range for all ℓ, by
   304	  the common V). Lemma 8.5′(R′) (§5) applies to each Q and each x ∈ 𝒳 (by (P8): q₀ − 2ν = μ − ν ≥ η₀ and
   305	  ξ/2 − q₀ ≥ η₀/2, ξ := μ + h + dν), and [pp] Corollary `cor:bad` gives
   306	  π_J^{−1}Σ_ℓ 𝔟_ℓ ≤ C|𝒳|ε(N)(MV/Y)ρ_r(log N)^{C}, with |𝒳| = O(log ϖ) = O(Λ) and
   307	  ε(N) = exp(−c u/log²u), u ≍ D^{2/5}. This is ≤ (log N)^{−C−5} times the good mass. ∎
