   314	## 5. Lemma 8.5′ in regime (R′)
   315	
   316	The hypothesis "y = ⌊L_N[1/2, a]⌋, log x/log N in a compact set" of [lem85] §1 is used in its proof only through
   317	the following consequences. We take them as the hypotheses.
   318	
   319	**Regime (R′)** (quantitative gaps; no fixed λ — repair after codex lv5unif_2 #1). Fix K₀ ≥ 1, and let U₀ ≥ 8 be an
   320	absolute constant such that the error term of Hildebrand–Tenenbaum's Theorem 3 is ≤ 1/100 for u ≥ U₀ − 1. Let y ≥ 2
   321	and x, Y, Q satisfy:
   322	- (R′1) log y ≥ 4(log log x)², (log x)^{c_D} ≤ y;
   323	- (R′2) u := log x/log y ≥ max((log log x)⁴, 4(2K₀ + 6)/η_D);
   324	- (R′3) u log(4u log y) ≤ K₀ log y;
   325	- (R′4) Y ≥ y^{K}, K := 2K₀ + 6, and the **level gap** Γ := min(log(Q/Y), log(√x/Q)) satisfies
   326	  Γ ≥ (2K₀ + U₀)log y + 4 log log x.
   327	
   328	**Lemma 8.5′(R′) [proved; re-check of [lem85]].** Under (R′), for x ≥ x₀(K₀),
   329	  Σ_{t∈𝒯_Q} max_{(r,t)=1}|Ψ(x, y; t, r) − Ψ_t(x, y)/φ(t)| ≤ C·Ψ(x, y)·δ_𝒯·ε,
   330	  ε := exp(−c u/log²(u + 1)) + y^{−1/2},
   331	and Qδ_𝒯/10 ≤ #𝒯_Q ≤ 3Qδ_𝒯 (δ_𝒯 = ϱ(Q/Y, y)/log Y), where C, c, x₀ depend only on K₀ and on absolute constants
   332	(Drappeau's η_D, c_D, δ_D, C_D; HT's; C_dBT, C_α).
   333	
   334	*Proof (every use of regime (R) and of λ in [lem85], replaced).*
   335	- (α1)/(α2) ([lem85] §2): 1 − β(z, y) ≤ (log(u log y) + C_α log log y)/log y ≤ 1/4 for 2y ≤ z ≤ x, by (R′1).
   336	- E7: ϱ(z, y) ≥ y^{−1}exp(−u_z log(4u_z log y)) ≥ y^{−1−K₀} for 2y ≤ z ≤ x, by (R′3) (u_z ≤ u). This replaces
   337	  "u log(4u log y) = (ξ/a²)(1 + o(1))log y".
   338	- Lemma SM (a): Drappeau's Lemme 5 at z = x/d ≥ x^{1/2} (d ≤ Q′ ≤ √x) needs (log z)^{c_D} ≤ y ≤ z and
   339	  R₁ = y^K ≤ z^{η_D}; the latter is K log y ≤ (η_D/2)log x, i.e. u ≥ 2K/η_D, which is (R′2). The transfer factor is
   340	  R₁^{1−β′} ≤ (log x)^{K(1+C_α)} by (α2). The saving exp(−δ_D(u/2)/log²(u/2 + 1)) beats (log x)^{K(1+C_α)+1}
   341	  because u/log²u ≥ (log log x)⁴/(16(log log log x)²) by (R′2).
   342	- Lemma SM (b) and Part 2: Corollary LS′ gives ≤ 1.5·10³π(y)(log x)²(y^{3/2}x/R + y^{1/2}x^{1/2}Q₀) with R = y^K and
   343	  Q₀ = Q′ (resp. R = Y and Q₀ = Q). The target is Ψ(x, y)ϱ(Q′, y) (resp. Ψ(x, y)δ_𝒯), and by E7 both are
   344	  ≥ x·y^{−2−2K₀}/log Y. Relative to the target, the first term is ≤ C(log x)³y^{2K₀+9/2}/R ≤ y^{−1/2} because
   345	  K = 2K₀ + 6 and Y ≥ y^K, and the second is ≤ C(log x)³y^{2K₀+7/2}·Q₀/√x ≤ C(log x)³y^{2K₀+7/2}e^{−Γ} ≤ y^{−1/2}
   346	  by (R′4) (this is the uniform saving codex lv5unif_2 #1 asks for).
   347	- Part 1: Lemma SM applies to Q′ = Q/ℓ, since 2y ≤ e^{Γ}/2 ≤ Q/(2Y) ≤ Q′ ≤ Q ≤ √x·e^{−Γ}.
   348	- (i), the count of 𝒯_Q: HT Theorem 3 at z = Q/(2ℓ) ≥ e^{Γ}/4 ≥ y^{U₀−1}, so u_z ≥ U₀ − 1, and α(z, y) ≥ 0.99 by (α2)
   349	  and (R′1); the constants 0.8 and 4.1 of [lem85] follow.
   350	- E2 (lift averaging), E3, E4, E5, E6, E8, Lemma LS, Perron: regime-free. ∎
   351	
   352	**In the design.** y = B, x ∈ 𝒳 (so log x = θ log N(1 + o(1)) and u ≍ D^{2/5}), Y as in §1, Q one of the dyadic
   353	values covering [MV/32, 2MV]. (R′1): log B ≍ Λ ≫ (log log N)². (R′2): u ≍ D^{2/5} ≫ (log log N)⁴.
   354	(R′3): u log(4u log B)/log B → (4/5)θ_F₀/a², so K₀ := 1 + ⌈θ₀/a²⌉ works. (R′4): log Y ≍ Λ_{3/5} ≫ K log B; and, for
   355	every x ∈ 𝒳 (log x ≥ (μ + h + dν)log N − 2 log ϖ) and every such Q,
   356	  log(Q/Y) ≥ (μ − ν)log N − O(Λ) ≥ η₀ log N − O(Λ),
   357	  log(√x/Q) ≥ ((h − μ + (d−2)ν)/2)log N − O(Λ) ≥ (η₀/2)log N − O(Λ)
   358	by the floors (P8). So Γ ≥ (η₀/2)log N − O(Λ), which exceeds (2K₀ + U₀)log B + 4 log log N by (P2). No step uses a
   359	fixed λ; the gap grows like (log N log log N)^{1/2}, and every constant depends only on K₀ = K₀(a, κ, d₀).
   360	Codex lv5unif_1 §1(b) notes that B = L_x[1/2, Θ(1)]; codex lv5unif_2 #1 notes that the earlier fixed-λ formulation did
   361	not justify the application with λ_N = η₀/(4ξ) → 0, which this version removes. ∎
