   422	## 7. Relation supply: γ ≥ (log N)^{−C_γ}
   423	
   424	**Theorem D-U [proved].** γ = Pr_{ℓ,A}[N_ℓ(A) ≥ 1] ≥ (log N)^{−C_γ} with C_γ = C(a, κ, d₀).
   425	*Proof.* Paley–Zygmund as in [pp] Theorem `thm:Dk`: with m = S²ρ_rρ_F, P₁ := d(log N)^{C_FM} and
   426	P₂ := dη₀^{−1}(log N)^{C_LD}, γ ≥ (E N)²/(E[N(N−1)] + E N) ≥ 1/(P₁²P₂ + P₁/m). By Lemma CS, m ≥ (log N)^{−2C_R}; and
   427	d ≤ log N, η₀^{−1} ≤ (log N)^{1/2}. So P₁²P₂ ≤ (log N)^{2C_FM+C_LD+4}, P₁/m ≤ 4(log N)^{C_FM+2C_R+1}, and
   428	C_γ := 2C_FM + C_LD + 2C_R + 5 works. ∎
   429	
   430	**Field rejections [proved; [pp] Lemma `lem:IR`, `lem:reject`].** Lemma IR's proof is uniform in d with the
   431	absolute prime threshold r₀ = 16 (the irreducible count ((r^d − 1)/(r − 1) − 2r^{d/2})/d ≥ r^{d−1}/(2d) holds for
   432	all d ≥ 3, r ≥ 16), and the near-uniformity factor (1 + Q_IR/(2H + 1))^d ≤ e needs Q_IR ≤ (2H+1)/d, true since
   433	Q_IR = H^{1/2+o(1)}. So Pr(𝓡) ≤ exp(−log H/(13d log log H)) + 3/(2H + 1) ≤ γ/2 by (P7). ∎
