   437	## 8. Split counting and field selection at growing k
   438	
   439	**Theorem K-U [proved].** Let A be a field returned by SAMPLE_FIELD with δ_A ≥ γ/4. Then one call of
   440	DESCEND_ONCE(A) returns a row or makes a factor exit with probability ≥ (δ_A/(4 log N))^{2k}/(32k²).
   441	*Proof.* |𝒟_A| ≥ γπ_J/4 ≥ 4k³2^{ω(N)} by (P6) and Theorem D-U. The products of k distinct primes of 𝒟_A lie in
   442	(Y^k, (2Y)^k] ⊂ (X2^{−2k}, X], so some window [Y′/2, Y′] of the 2k dyadic windows holds a set 𝒮 of
   443	≥ C(|𝒟_A|, k)/(2k) of them, with 2Y′² < N. Lemma S″ ([rec] §3.2) gives Pr_R[E] ≥ |𝒮|²/(2φ(N)) for R uniform on
   444	Q_N, with E: the primitive vector of Λ_R is ±(u, v), u, v ∈ 𝒮 coprime. So Pr_r[E] ≥ |𝒮|²/(2N). With
   445	|𝒮| ≥ (|𝒟_A|/k)^k/(2k), |𝒟_A| ≥ δ_AY/(2 log Y), Y^{2k} ≥ N/(4·16^k) and 2k log Y ≤ log N, this is
   446	≥ (δ_A/(4 log N))^{2k}/(32k²). On E the shape test passes (exactly k distinct primes of 𝒟_A ⊂ J on each side) and
   447	every special-q search returns an atom ([pp] Prop `prop:BS`). ∎
   448	
   449	*Remarks.* No 2^{−ω(N)} (Theorem S′'s loss; 2^ω can be L_N[3/5]^{Θ(1/log log N)}, far above L[2/5]) and no
   450	C(2k, k) (S′'s c_k). The shape-test waste ratio of Theorem K(iii) is not used: every attempt is charged a full
   451	shape test and 2k special-q searches ([rec] §3.2, codex recurse_2).
   452	
   453	**Proposition select-U [proved; sharper than [pp] Prop `prop:select`(ii)].** Let p be the probability that one trial
   454	(SAMPLE_FIELD + DESCEND_ONCE) ends in a factor exit or a row, C_trial a uniform bound on the expected cost of a
   455	trial or of one DESCEND_ONCE, and T_post that of POSTPROCESS. Then
   456	(i) p ≥ (γ/4)(γ/(16 log N))^{2k}/(32k²); (ii) E[cost of SPLIT] ≤ (2M_rows + 1)C_trial/p + 2T_post.
   457	*Proof.* (i): [pp] Prop `prop:select`(i) with Theorem K-U and the set 𝒢* = {A ∉ 𝓡 : δ_A ≥ γ/4} of measure ≥ γ/4.
   458	(ii): selection costs ≤ C_trial/p (Wald). The kept field A* has law ς_A𝒜(dA)/b, and given A* = A the expected cost
   459	is ≤ 2(M_rowsC_trial/ς_A + T_post) (≤ 2 expected rounds, Theorem DD). Averaging,
   460	(b/p)·2(M_rowsC_trial E[1/ς_{A*}] + T_post) ≤ 2M_rowsC_trial/p + 2T_post, since E[1/ς_{A*}] ≤ 1/b and b ≤ p.
   461	([pp] divides T_post by p too; at L[1/2] that was harmless, here it would add s to the 2a term.) ∎
