   465	## 9. LV6 at growing degree
   466	
   467	[pp] §8 (= lv6 Prop LV6, transferred by ldbound §6.1) is stated for fixed d. Its constants, re-checked:
   468	
   469	- **Lemma C, rows, columns:** degree-free. Computing the roots of f mod r for all r ≤ B costs π(B)·poly(d, log B).
   470	- **Lemma H:** log₂|H| ≤ d log₂|D| + d + ½log₂|disc g| + (d−1)log₂(d + log₂|disc g|). With ‖f‖_∞ ≤ 3MH
   471	  (Lemma GB_w and (P2)): log|D| = log|f_d disc f| = O(d(μ + h)log N + d log d) = O(log N), since d(μ + h) = O(dθ) = O(1);
   472	  and disc g = f_d^{(d−1)(d−2)}disc f gives log|disc g| = O(d²(μ + h)log N + d log d) = O(d log N) (codex lv5unif_2 #5).
   473	  So log|H| = O(d log N) and t_χ := ⌈5d(ln|H|_bd + 2 ln log N)⌉ = O(d² log N). Polynomial.
   474	- **Lemma E (≤ 1 exceptional class per field):** valid for every odd d. Stark's Lemma 8 with c(L) = 4(2d)! for
   475	  L_h = K(√h) (non-normal over Q); Landau with conductors ≤ Δ̄^{1/d}.
   476	- **The factorial threshold and its repair [proved].** ν₁ = min(1/(4(2d)! log Δ̄), c_L/(2 log Δ̄)). Lemma X needs the
   477	  exceptional term 2x^{1−ν₁} to be ≤ x/(40 log x), i.e. ν₁ log x ≥ log(80 log x). The old choice
   478	  log x ≈ (log N)² fails as soon as (2d)! ≫ log N. Take
   479	    s := log x := ⌈(2d)!·(log N + log Δ̄ + d)⁴⌉ (codex's choice; ours was 8(2d)!(log Δ̄)² + (log N)²).
   480	  Then ν₁s ≥ (log N + log Δ̄)³/(4 log Δ̄) ≫ log(80s) = O(d log d + log log N), and LO's conditions
   481	  s ≥ 20d(log Δ̄)² (log x ≥ 10n_L(log d_L)², n_L = 2d) and c₁x·exp(−c₂s^{1/2}/√(2d)) ≤ x/(40 log x) hold. The base-field
