   550	## 11. The shared-rational-side multi-field trick
   551	
   552	**Design MF.** One rational side g (as before) and J_f independent algebraic sides (w_j, c_j), j ≤ J_f, giving
   553	F_j := F̂_{g,w_j} + G·R_{c_j}, all with F_j(g₀, g₁) = Nw_j and the common root m = g₀/g₁ mod N. (w_j = 1, i.e. design
   554	(a″_k), also works: Lemma W is not needed.) A prime ℓ is MF-descendable if some P ∈ 𝒫 ∩ Λ_ℓ(g) has Y_P = 1
   555	(rational, filtered) and F_j(P) ∈ 𝒮_B for some j.
   556	
   557	**Design MF, with an extra height floor.** As above, and additionally H ≥ exp(13(σ + 1)·d·Λ·log log N) (that is,
   558	h ≥ h_*(μ) + η₀ + 13(σ + 1)dΛ log log N/log N; the extra term is ≍ (log N)^{−2/5}(log log N)^{7/5} = o(θ), so it does
   559	not move the exponent). This is needed because the pointwise bound below concerns raw fields, and post-processing needs
   560	accepted ones (codex lv5unif_2 #3: in the kernel-binding regime Lemma IR's rejection bound exp(−log H/(13d log log H))
   561	= exp(−Θ(D^{2/5})) is far *larger* than ρ_F = exp(−Θ(D^{2/5}log log N)), so without the extra floor all the
   562	pointwise smoothness mass could sit in rejected fields).
   563	
   564	**Proposition MF [moment part proved; multi-field post-processing proved in outline].** Let
   565	γ_r := Pr_{g,ℓ}[∃P ∈ 𝒫 ∩ Λ_ℓ(g) with Y_P = 1 and |G(P)| good]. If J_f ≥ 4(log N)^{C_g}/ρ_F, then
   566	  γ_MF := Pr[ℓ is MF-descendable through an *accepted* field] ≥ γ_r/2,  and  γ_r ≥ (log N)^{−C}.
   567	*Proof.*
   568	- **Decoupling.** Condition on (g, ℓ) and on the event that some P has Y_P = 1 with t = |G(P)| good; let P₀ be the
   569	  first such P in a fixed order (a function of (g, ℓ)). By Lemma GM-U, for every w_j,
   570	  Pr_{c_j}[F_j(P₀) ∈ 𝒮_B] ≥ ρ_F/(log N)^{C_g} =: p₁ (its residue c_{P₀}w_j is a unit, [pp] Lemma `lem:coprime`). The
   571	  rejection event of field j depends on (g, w_j, c_j) only, and by Lemma IR (stated for fixed g, w, with c uniform) and
   572	  [pp] Lemma `lem:reject`, Pr_{c_j}[rejected | g, w_j] ≤ exp(−log H/(13d log log H)) + 3/(2H + 1) + 1/W ≤ p₁/2 by
   573	  the extra floor. So Pr_{c_j}[F_j(P₀) ∈ 𝒮_B and field j accepted | g, ℓ, w_j] ≥ p₁/2. (A field that makes a factor
   574	  exit ends the algorithm successfully.) The pairs (w_j, c_j) are independent of each other and of (g, ℓ), so
   575	  Pr[no accepted j with F_j(P₀) smooth | g, ℓ] ≤ (1 − p₁/2)^{J_f} ≤ e^{−2} < 1/2.
   576	- **The rational moment.** N_r^{good} := #{P : Y_P = 1, t good}. E N_r^{good} ≥ E N_r/2 ≥ S²ρ_r/(log N)^C (the
   577	  rational part of FM-U, with the bad-mass bound of §4), and E[N_r^{good}(N_r^{good} − 1)] ≤ E[N_r(N_r − 1)] ≤
   578	  (log N)^C S⁴ρ_r² ([pp] Prop `prop:R` = Theorem R; it is rational-only and uniform: Lemma `lem:reg` gives ≤ 200S²
   579	  partners, and its divisor switching is DS-U). With S² ≥ (log N)^{−C}/ρ_r (the rational-only analogue of Lemma CS),
   580	  Paley–Zygmund gives γ_r ≥ (log N)^{−C}. ∎
   581	- **Why no algebraic second moment is needed.** The one-point bound is a statement about one fixed candidate, and
   582	  independence across fields turns it into a probability. Codex lv5unif_1 §2 gives a different valid argument
   583	  (conditional PZ on the full count, needing an averaged algebraic second moment with exp(o(Λ)) loss, and only
   584	  exp(o(Λ)) fields). Its counterexample — fields that all succeed on the same deterministic target set — is
   585	  excluded here by the pointwise lower bound p₁ > 0 at every (g, ℓ) with a good rational candidate.
   586	- **Post-processing with J_f fields (outline, repaired after codex lv5unif_2 #4).**
   587	  - Columns: the shared rational ones (sign, p ≤ B), and for each field j its parity, (r, s) and character columns.
   588	    Per field, t_χ^{(j)} := ⌈5d(ln|H_j|_bd + 2 ln log N + ln(4J_f))⌉ characters, so that, by Lemma X and a union bound,
   589	    with probability ≥ 3/4 every field has |H_{j,0}| ≤ 2 simultaneously. Rows: M_rows ≥ C_col^{MF} + J_f + 12, so the
   590	    kernel has dimension ≥ J_f + 12.
   591	  - Linearity: φ_j is F₂-linear on the kernel K of all columns (Lemma H's φ, restricted), with values in H_{j,0}. On
   592	    the event |H_{j,0}| ≤ 2, H_{j,0} ⊂ F₂, so b_j(s) := [Γ_{j,s} is not a square] = φ_j(s) is an F₂-linear functional
   593	    on K.
   594	  - Take J_f + 2 independent uniform kernel vectors s_i (independent with probability ≥ 1 − 2^{−9}); compute the
   595	    J_f × (J_f + 2) bit matrix b_j(s_i) with Algorithm SQ in each field; take a nonzero x in its right kernel (it
   596	    exists, J_f equations in J_f + 2 unknowns) and S := Σx_is_i ≠ 0. Then φ_j(S) = 0 for every j, i.e. every field's
   597	    product is a square. **Verify exactly** with SQ in every field; on failure (characters bad for some field),
   598	    resample characters and kernel vectors. Expected O(1) repetitions; Las Vegas.
