   602	- **Cost and exponent.** J_f = L^{σ_F + o(1)}, σ_F := log(1/ρ_F)/Λ. Per special-q: ≤ 200S_r² rational values with
   603	  S_r² ≈ 1/ρ_r, then J_f algebraic values for each of ≈ S_r²ρ_r rationally smooth candidates. All exponents are
   604	  finite, so Theorem U's conclusion α = 2/5 also follows from Proposition MF, with a different constant, once the
   605	  outlined post-processing is written in full. **The trick does not lower α**: (R1) and (R3) of §13 are unchanged.
   606	
