   160	## 2. Smooth-number inputs in the new range
   161	
   162	Throughout, z is **in range** if B^{D^{1/3}} ≤ z ≤ N. Every argument of ϱ used below is in range: the smallest is
   163	X_r B^{−2C₀−1}, with log X_r/log B ≍ D^{2/5}.
   164	
   165	**Lemma U1 (local behaviour of ϱ) [proved].** For N ≥ N₀ and z₁ ≤ z₂ ≤ z₁B^{C} with z₁ in range:
   166	(i) ϱ(z₂) ≤ 2ϱ(z₁); (ii) ϱ(z₁) ≤ (log N)^{C_U(C+1)}ϱ(z₂), with C_U absolute;
   167	(iii) for fixed Z ≥ 1, Ψ(z₁(1 + 1/Z)) − Ψ(z₁) ≥ Ψ(z₁)/(3Z), and Ψ(z₁/2) ≥ Ψ(z₁)/3;
   168	(iv) log(1/ϱ(z)) = u_z log u_z (1 + o(1)), u_z = log z/log B.
   169	
   170	*Proof.* As [pp] Lemma `lem:local`, whose proof uses only Hildebrand–Tenenbaum's Theorems 2(i) and 3 and u → ∞:
   171	(1 − α(z, B))log B = log log z − log(1 + log z/B) + O(log log B) ≤ log log N + C log log B, so
   172	B^{1 − α} ≤ (log N)^{1+C}; and 1/u_z ≤ D^{−1/3} → 0 uniformly in range. (iv) is Canfield–Erdős–Pomerance, valid
   173	since u_z ≤ log z/(2 log log z) for z in range (here u_z ≍ D^{2/5} while log z/log log z ≫ D^{4/5} for z ≥ X_r^{1/2}). ∎
   174	
   175	**Lemma CS (a computable S with m := S²ρ_rρ_F polylogarithmic) [proved].** For z in range let α̂(z) be the root of
   176	Σ_{p≤B} log p/(p^α − 1) = log z, computed by bisection to absolute accuracy (log N)^{−3}, and
   177	R(z) := z^{α̂−1}∏_{p≤B}(1 − p^{−α̂})^{−1}, computed to relative accuracy 2. Then
   178	  R*(z)/2 ≤ R(z) ≤ 2R*(z), where R*(z) := z^{α̂−1}∏_{p≤B}(1 − p^{−α̂})^{−1} exactly, and
   179	  ϱ(z) ≤ R*(z) ≤ (log N)^{C_R}ϱ(z)   (C_R absolute).
   180	Moreover (existence, proved first, without using the size of S): uniformly for 1 ≤ S² ≤ e^{2σΛ},
   181	  log(R(X_r(S))R(X_F(S))) = −σΛ(1 + o(1)),  σ := 2θ₀/(5a).
   182	Hence the scan of §1 (S = 2^j for j = 0, 1, 2, …, stopping at the first success; there is no binary search and no
   183	monotonicity assumption) stops at some S with S² ≤ e^{(σ+o(1))Λ}; at that S, (log N)^{−2C_R}/4 ≤ m ≤ 64. Computing S
   184	costs O(Λ)·π(B)(log N)^{O(1)} = B^{1+o(1)}.
   185	
   186	*Proof.*
   187	- **Upper bound (Rankin).** For every α ∈ (0, 1], Ψ(z, B) ≤ Σ_{P⁺(n)≤B}(z/n)^α = z^α∏_{p≤B}(1 − p^{−α})^{−1}.
   188	- **Lower bound.** Hildebrand–Tenenbaum 1986, Theorem 1: Ψ(z, B) = z^{α}ζ(α, B)/(α√(2πφ₂(α, B)))·(1 + O(1/u + log B/B))
   189	  uniformly for z ≥ B ≥ 2, at the saddle point α = α(z, B), with φ₂(α, B) = Σ_{p≤B} p^α(log p)²/(p^α − 1)²
   190	  ≍ log z·log B. So the Rankin value at α exceeds ϱ(z) by the factor α√(2πφ₂)(1 + o(1)) ≤ log N. The function
   191	  g(α′) := log(z^{α′}ζ(α′, B)) is convex with g′(α) = 0 and g″ = φ₂. For |α′ − α| ≤ 1/log B every term of φ₂ changes by
   192	  a factor ≤ e³, so if |α̂ − α| ≤ (log N)^{−3}, then g(α̂) − g(α) ≤ e³φ₂(α)(log N)^{−6}/2 ≤ 1. Bisection is valid
   193	  because the defining sum is decreasing in α. Hence R*(z) ≤ e·log N·ϱ(z)(1 + o(1)); take C_R := 2 if HT's implied
   194	  constant is absorbed, and in general C_R absolute.
   195	- **Existence (codex lv5unif_2 #2).** For 1 ≤ S² ≤ e^{2σΛ}, d log S ≤ dσΛ = o(θ log N) directly from the growth
   196	  rates d ≍ D^{1/5}, Λ = D^{2/5}λ, θ log N ≍ D^{4/5}λ; so log X_r + log X_F = θ log N(1 + o(1)) uniformly on this range,
   197	  and Lemma U1(iv) with the bounds ϱ ≤ R* ≤ (log N)^{C_R}ϱ gives the displayed asymptotic. At S² = e^{(σ+ε)Λ} the
   198	  product S²R_rR_F is therefore ≥ e^{(ε+o(1))Λ} ≥ 1, so the scan stops at or before that S. This argument uses
   199	  nothing about the S where the scan stops, which removes the circularity of the first draft.
   200	- **m.** At the chosen S, S²R(X_r)R(X_F) ≥ 1, so m = S²ρ_rρ_F ≥ S²R*_rR*_F(log N)^{−2C_R} ≥ S²R_rR_F/(4(log N)^{2C_R})
   201	  ≥ (log N)^{−2C_R}/4. If S ≥ 2, the inequality failed at S/2, so
   202	  S² < 4/(R_r(S/2)R_F(S/2)) ≤ 16/(R*_r(S/2)R*_F(S/2)) ≤ 16/(ρ_r(S/2)ρ_F(S/2)) ≤ 64/(ρ_r(S)ρ_F(S)),
   203	  using Lemma U1(i) (X(S/2) ≤ X(S) ≤ 2^{d+1}X(S/2) ≤ BX(S/2)). So m ≤ 64. (If S = 1, m ≤ 1 trivially.) The value
   204	  of σ: u log u summed over the two sides is (θ₀/a)D^{2/5}·(2/5)λ(1 + o(1)) = σΛ(1 + o(1)).
   205	- **Why S^d must be inside X_F.** S^d = B^{Θ(d)}, and a shift of the argument of ϱ by B^{Θ(d)} changes ϱ by
   206	  (log N)^{Θ(d)} (Lemma U1(ii) with C ≍ d). Evaluating ρ_F at the box size without S would therefore manufacture
   207	  a (log N)^{Θ(d)} = τ = 1 discrepancy (codex lv5unif_1 §1 (2) makes the same point). The scan over S = 2^j evaluates
   208	  R at the actual X_F(S) each time; the map S ↦ S²R(X_r(S))R(X_F(S)) is not assumed monotone. ∎
   209	
   210	*Remark.* thmA's explicit S² = ⌈L^{θ/(2a)}⌉ gave only m = L^{o(1)} (thmA U5); at L[1/2] that sufficed. At L[2/5]
   211	the split raises γ to the power 2k ≍ D^{2/5}, so m must be polylogarithmic, and Lemma CS is needed.
