   503	## 10. Recursion at Λ_{2/5} and Theorem U
   504	
   505	**Lemma F_α [proved; [rec] Lemma F with √2 replaced by 2^α].** Let 0 < α < 1 and L_x := exp(Λ_α(x)) with
   506	Λ_α(x) := (log x)^α(max(1, log log x))^{1−α}. If F: [2, ∞) → [0, ∞) is nondecreasing and finite and, for x ≥ x₀,
   507	F(x) ≤ L_x^{p+ε(x)} + L_x^{δ+ε(x)}F(√(2x)) with ε(x) → 0, then F(x) ≤ L_x^{c+o(1)}, c := max(p, δ/(1 − 2^{−α})).
   508	*Proof.* Scaling: for y = √(2x), (log y)^α ≤ 2^{−α}(log x)^α + α2^{−α}(log 2)(log x)^{α−1} and log log y ≤ log log x, so
   509	Λ_α(y) ≤ 2^{−α}Λ_α(x) + o(1) and L_y^b ≤ e·L_x^{2^{−α}b} for x ≥ x₁(b). Then [rec]'s steps 2–5 verbatim with
   510	η′ := η(1 − 2^{−α})/4: in step 4 the second exponent is δ + η′ + (c + η)2^{−α} ≤ c + η2^{−α} + η′ = c + η − 3η′. ∎
   511	
   512	**The recursion inequality.** Let F(x) := sup_{2≤n≤x} E[cost of FACTOR_U(n)]. Finiteness holds by the alternation
   513	with trial division ([rec] §1.1 item 3). For x ≥ x₀, by [rec]'s accounting (factor tree with ≤ 2log₂x nodes,
   514	Lemma W of [rec] for adaptive sub-calls, Lemma OS for oracle substitution) and Proposition select-U:
   515	  F(x) ≤ 2log₂x·[P(x) + D(x)·F(√(2x))],
   516	  P(x) = L_x^{max(2a, a + s + max(a, σ)) + o(1)},  D(x) = 2(2M_rows + 1)/p = L_x^{a + s + o(1)},   (10.1)
   517	with s := 2κ(1 + C_γ), because:
   518	- M_rows ≤ (d + 1)π(B) + O(d² log N) = L^{a+o(1)};
   519	- 1/p ≤ 4γ^{−1}(16 log N/γ)^{2k}·32k² = exp((2k + 1)(log 16 + (1 + C_γ)log log N) + O(log k)) = L^{s+o(1)},
   520	  since 2k log log N = 2κΛ(1 + o(1));
   521	- C_trial = 2F(√(2N)) [shape test] + 2k·T_SQ + (log N)^{O(1)}poly(d), with T_SQ = Õ(B + S²) = L^{max(a,σ)+o(1)}
   522	  ([pp] Prop `prop:BS`; the batch has ≤ 200S²·2 numbers of ≤ log X_F = O(log N) bits);
   523	- T_post = L^{2a+o(1)} (Prop LV6-U); preprocessing L^{a+o(1)}; S costs B^{1+o(1)} (Lemma CS).
   524	
   525	**Theorem U [proved, conditional as stated in the Verdict].** For fixed rationals a, κ, d₀ > 0, FACTOR_U[a, κ, d₀] is
   526	Las Vegas and completely factors every N ≥ 2 in expected time L_N[2/5, c + o(1)] with
   527	  c = max(2a, a + s + max(a, σ), (a + s)/(1 − 2^{−2/5})),  s = 2κ(1 + C_γ),  σ = 2θ₀(d₀, κ)/(5a).   (10.3)
   528	*Proof.* Lemma F_α with α = 2/5 applied to (10.1); the 2log₂x factors are L^{o(1)}. Correctness: AKS-certified primes;
   529	almost-sure termination from the finite expectation. ∎
