  1748	the maximal order at $r$, and by Dedekind--Kummer the primes above $r$ correspond to the irreducible factors $\phi_j$ of $f\bmod r$ and are
  1749	unramified. (i) $F_A(a,b)\equiv f_da^d\not\equiv0$, and $a-b\alpha\equiv a$ modulo every $\fp\mid r$. (ii) $a-b\alpha\in\fp_j$ iff
  1750	$\phi_j(ab^{-1})\equiv0$, i.e.\ iff $\phi_j=x-ab^{-1}$. Since $\Norm(a-b\alpha)=F_A(a,b)/f_d$ and $\fp$ has degree one,
  1751	$\ord_\fp(a-b\alpha)=v_r(F_A(a,b))$. For the consequence: primes $r>B$ with $r\nmid D$ contribute nothing, since $F_A(P)$ is $B$-smooth.
  1752	\end{proof}
