  1831	\emph{Characters.} A degree-one prime $\fp=(r,\alpha-s)$ with $r\nmid D$ defines a quadratic character on $\sH$: $\chi_\fp(\fq):=$ the
  1832	Legendre symbol modulo $\fp$ of the $\fp$-unit $\gamma\pi^{-\ord_\fp\gamma}$, for a representative $\gamma\in V_D$ and a uniformiser $\pi$ at $\fp$. Since
  1833	$\ord_\fp\gamma$ is even, this does not depend on $\pi$, and it is well defined on $V_D/K^{\times2}$.
  1834	On atoms, $\chi_\fp(a-b\alpha)=\bigl((a-bs)/r\bigr)$. The character columns are $\sum_\ell e_{i\ell}(1-\chi_{\fp_j}(a_{P_\ell}-b_{P_\ell}\alpha))/2\bmod2$,
  1835	for independent samples $\fp_1,\dots,\fp_{t_\chi}$.
