  1848	The error term is $2c_1x\exp(-c_2\log N/\sqrt{2d})=o(x/\log x)$, as $\log x=O((\log N)^2)$. Primes of degree $\ge2$ and ramified primes are
  1849	negligible. There are at most $d(\pi(x)-\pi(x/2))\le0.6dx/\log x$ degree-one primes in all, so the ratio is at least $1/(5d)$. Independence and a
